{"title":"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_26\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 26</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Infinite_Series)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Infinite Series)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Probability_States)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Probability States)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_26\">Problem 26</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 26\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alice, Bob, and Carol repeatedly take turns tossing a die. Alice begins; Bob always follows Alice; Carol always follows Bob; and Alice always follows Carol. Find the probability that Carol will be the first one to toss a six. (The probability of obtaining a six on any toss is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55ed481f94445cc6cf731c6585a80ede1608cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, independent of the outcome of any other toss.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23fe40796d371cac763c12a863be3cf8c0169314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{9}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{18}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{25}{91}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{36}{91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"394\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Infinite_Series.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Infinite_Series)\">Solution 1 (Infinite Series)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Infinite Series)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For Carol to win on her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> roll, the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68eabcc9922cdddf961b463f94a8b64d0fecbd42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> rolls must not be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the last roll must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the probability that Carol wins on her <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa62a365c27d4f2c298262b3e8c7c224550c20a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{th}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> roll is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7727625ec82805795fea033f95904224ade2d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^{3n-1} = \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{125}{216}\\right)^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"217\" height=\"48\" />.  Taking the sum of this expression over all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, her total probability of winning must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc7a961015ce0656fd6f93d94cabd206ac6adec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{125}{216}\\right)^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"123\" height=\"53\" />.  Since this is a geometric series with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/5476ba137618ce048cfc5c14f66826ed6ed06f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{216}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> and common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c9f313bc1f40d0a99f14dbf6bdf49ab30cdde6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{125}{216}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, Carol's probability of winning is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f729df1831a4f299cb3a13d6107d433e95253db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{25}{216}}{1-\\frac{125}{216}}=\\frac{\\frac{25}{216}}{\\frac{91}{216}}=\\frac{25}{91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"159\" height=\"49\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4003a21b78c8ecdf40aef519713be4d9daa7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Probability_States.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Probability_States)\">Solution 2 (Probability States)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Probability States)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be Carol's probabilities of winning, depending on whether it is Alice's, Bob's or Carol's turn to roll the die next, respectively.  Since it is initially Alice's turn, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> will be the answer.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9fc2a2aa04e0d7240d2b0fb980faaf9fb5a9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{5}{6}b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8489cae72f3f093c1dc66abea870aa70190bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{5}{6}c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/936daf3fc751def8b3cfd49bce8599d08a46a413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{5}{6}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />.  Substituting into the first equation shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c79d71fe4f72e25310ced06cf93e764f330bc765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{5}{6}b = \\frac{25}{36}c = \\frac{25}{36}\\left(\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{5}{6}a\\right) = \\frac{25}{216} + \\frac{125}{216}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"363\" height=\"45\" />. Solving the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4dacc8a24409357f63b4f13e85beff5db7faa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{25}{216} + \\frac{125}{216}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90adaedaec9d742fe75d95c42e26d8e90bb0d019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{25}{91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd4003a21b78c8ecdf40aef519713be4d9daa7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" /> \n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME\" title=\"1981 AHSME\">1981 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1981 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1981\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit